# Normalise line endings.
#
# Four people on four laptops, at least one of them Windows. Without this, git
# converts LF to CRLF on checkout, and the mutation harnesses match multi-line
# snippets against file contents -- so a CRLF checkout would silently report
# SKIP for every multi-line mutation, which looks like coverage while measuring
# nothing. Both harnesses defend against that in code (`localise`), and this
# removes the need to.
#
# It also keeps the SHA-256 restore verification meaningful across machines.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
